# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Java (deploy/graphhopper/lts-wrapper)
target/
*.class

# Node (ui/)
node_modules/
ui/dist/
ui/.vite/

# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.local
*.local.yaml

# Personal run history. Scope 3.7 is local-first: raw activity files are read where they
# sit, never copied, and only derived curves are kept. `.gitattributes` has marked these
# binary since M0, which is not the same as refusing to commit one.
*.fit
*.tcx
# A Strava bulk export gzips its originals and names its archive `export_<id>.zip`. Plain
# `.gpx` cannot be ignored - every golden route is one - so only the compressed forms are.
*.fit.gz
*.tcx.gz
*.gpx.gz
export_*.zip

# Local run artifacts
*.log
scratch/

# UI build output and its lockfile-managed deps. `ui/dist` is what `longrun api --ui`
# serves and is produced by `npm run build`; committing it would put a minified bundle in
# every diff. `node_modules/` and `ui/dist/` were already listed above; this adds the
# local vite cache directories npm 11 writes.
ui/node_modules/
ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# Plans written by `longrun plan --out` and served by `longrun api --plans`. A stored
# plan is a run of somebody's, not a fixture: the goldens are where a plan this project
# tests against belongs, and one committed here would be a sixth golden nobody reviewed.
plans/

# What the M15 browser suite leaves behind: `test-results/` holds the trace Playwright
# keeps for a failed gesture, `playwright-report/` the viewer for it. Both are a record of
# one run on one machine. The suite's own scratch - the seeded plan and the server's
# `plans/` directory - is written under the system temp directory and never inside the
# tree, which is the rule immediately above applied rather than worked around.
ui/test-results/
ui/playwright-report/
